+raw_text = "~ first_meeting
+set voice = \"voicetick4\"
+Zip: Hey there! my name is Zip.
+Zip: You look like you just woke from a [i]deep[/i] sleep!
+Zip: There’s just a few things you gotta know about this place. Looks like you already discovered that you can [color=green]jump[/color] with [action=jump]!
+Zip: Be sure to hold the jump button to get the most height you can out of it.
+Zip: You can also zoom in using [action=zoom_in], and zoom out using [action=zoom_out]!
+Zip: And remember, play at your own pace!
+set GlobalFlags.zip_done_first_meeting = true
+=> END
+# Taught Jump & Marble
+
+~ first_magnet_wall
+set voice = \"voicetick4\"
+Zip: This is a magnet wall.
+Zip: You see, when you’re a marble… you’re [i]incredibly[/i] magnetic.
+Zip: Press [action=do_marble] to [color=green]toggle marble mode[/color]! You’ll be on a roll in no time.
+set GlobalFlags.zip_done_first_magnet_wall = true
+=> END
+
+~ wall_controls
+set voice = \"voicetick4\"
+if not GlobalFlags.zip_done_wall_controls_explanation:
+	set GlobalFlags.zip_done_wall_controls_explanation = true
+	Zip: If you find wall movement to be unexpected, there's an alternate directional mapping in the [color=purple]Controls Settings![/color]
+	Zip: Would you like me to toggle it for you?
+else:
+	Zip: Would you like me to toggle the directional mapping setting?
+- Yes
+	set Settings.control_mapping_option = not Settings.control_mapping_option
+	set GlobalFlags.zip_switched_wall_controls_count = GlobalFlags.zip_switched_wall_controls_count + 1
+	if Settings.control_mapping_option == 0:
+		Zip: Set to [b][color=purple]Camera Relative[/color][/b]
+	else:
+		Zip: Set to [b][color=purple]Surface Fixed[/color][/b]
+	if not Settings.marble_arrow_enabled and GlobalFlags.zip_switched_wall_controls_count > 2:
+		Zip: If it still doesn't feel right, I can also make your input direction visible while magnetized.
+		- Sure
+			set Settings.marble_arrow_enabled = true
+			Zip: I set Marble Arrow Enabled to [color=green]true[/color].
+			Zip: You can disable this anytime in the [color=purple]Accesibility Settings[/color].
+		- No.
+- No thanks.
+=> END
+
+~ marble_jumping
+set voice = \"voicetick4\"
+Zip: If you chain a series of jumps together while you’re a marble, you will jump higher and higher!
+Zip: Use this information to escae the pull of magnets!
+set GlobalFlags.zip_done_marble_jumping = true
+=> END
+
+#~ respawn
+#set voice = \"voicetick4\"
+#Zip: Press [action=respawn] to 
+#set GlobalFlags.zip_done_marble_bounce = true
+
+~ sprinting
+set voice = \"voicetick4\"
+Zip: Hey I forgot to mention...
+Zip: When you're going [i]really[/i] fast as marble, try [color=green]unmarbling[/color] to take tighter corners.
+#Zip: Then again... if you're running you'll slowly lose momentum.
+#Zip: Do with that information what you will.
+#Zip: When you're going [i]really[/i] fast as marble, you can't turn corners very easily.
+#Zip: Then again... if you stay unmarbled for too long you'll eventually slow down
+Zip: [tornado radius=1.0 freq=1.0 connected=1]Buuuut,[/tornado] you will slowly lose speed, so don't stay as a guy forever.
+Zip: Do with that information what you will.
+#Zip: If you chain a series of jumps together while you’re a marble, you will jump higher and higher!
+#Zip: Use this information to bounce even higher than before!
+set GlobalFlags.zip_done_sprinting = true
+=> END
+
+~ data_lens
+set voice = \"voicetick4\"
+Zip: You have now acquired the [color=light_blue]Data Lens[/color]!
+Zip: You can access the [color=light_blue]Data Lens[/color] by opening it in the taskbar in the bottom left. [color=green]Click once[/color] to free your cursor and open the taskbar!
+Zip: The [color=light_blue]Data Lens[/color] reveals secrets behind it that cannot normally be seen - objects that are [color=blue]invisible[/color] unless seen through its frame.
+Zip: You can drag and resize the [color=light_blue]Data Lens[/color] window to get a better look!
+set GlobalFlags.zip_done_data_lens = false
+=> END
+
+~ familiar_platforming
+set voice = \"voicetick4\"
+Zip: What a strange land!
+Zip: It looks... strangely familiar...
+Zip: Do you remember this place?
+- I've seen it before
+	Zip: ;)
+- uhh
+	Zip: Don't worry about it!
+set GlobalFlags.zip_done_familiar_platforming = true
+=> END
+
+~ long_jump
+set voice = \"voicetick4\"
+Zip: Hey thanks for playing our demo!
+Zip: That's pretty much everything we can show you for now...
+Zip: But you're welcome to stick around and keep exploring!
+Zip: There may be some secrets you missed. ;)
+Zip: I'll leave you with one more tip:
+Zip: If you jump while holding [action=do_marble], you'll perform a long jump!
+Zip: You can even do it in the air!
+Zip: Have fun!~
+set GlobalFlags.zip_done_long_jump = true
+=> END
+
+~ bhopping
+set voice = \"voicetick4\"
+Zip: You seem like you enjoy breaking the rules...
+Zip: I have another tip for you.
+Zip: If you do a really short jump, you'll [color=light_blue]b[/color] able to strafe around in the air like crazy!
+Zip: I call it [color=light_blue]b-hopping[/color]! What do u think?
+- I feel like it's been done before...
+	Zip: Oh... :L
+- Very cool!
+	Zip: Thanks I invented it.
+set GlobalFlags.zip_done_bhopping = true
+=> END"
+metadata/dialogue_manager_version = "3.7.1"
